==========================================================================
PART 2 -- THE CENTRAL LEMMA: SEPARATE CONSERVATION
==========================================================================

  Bianchi:  grad^mu G_{mu nu} = 0.  From (I), grad^mu(T^m + T^phi)_{mu nu} = 0.
  Matter couples to g only  =>  grad^mu T^m_{mu nu} = 0 (standard).
  Hence                        grad^mu T^phi_{mu nu} = 0.

  THE DARK FLUID IS SEPARATELY CONSERVED.

  [PASS] F2 [THE LEMMA] grad^mu T^phi_{mu nu} = 0 follows from Bianchi plus
      minimal coupling -- so the dark fluid does not exchange energy with
      baryons: it is a distinct, collisionless component
         measured: grad(T^m + T^phi) = 0 and grad T^m = 0  =>  grad T^phi = 0
         THIS IS WHY DARK MATTER LOOKS LIKE A SEPARATE SUBSTANCE WITHOUT BEING
         ONE. The separate conservation is a theorem of the field
         equations, not evidence for a particle.

